            "type": "keyword",
            "ecs": true
          }
        ],
        "setup": "## Data requirements - S2\n\n- Sysmon event IDs consumed by the query: 1.\n- Channel: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational.\n- Detection basis: \nDetection basis: Sigma PowerShell flag corpus (name-referenced); MITRE T1059.001. A command-line/context signal, not proof of script contents; overlap with S3/R2 for the WMI consumer is documented (one event, two signals).\n\nBuilding block (building_block_type=default): hidden from the default alert view, feeds correlation; no signal alone asserts an incident.\nVerify the installed integration: event.category, field types, casing, null handling and source-to-ECS mapping against actual events. required_fields is descriptive metadata, not a mapping check. The public export retains the original broad index patterns - scope them to verified data streams in the destination environment.\nQuery interpretation and evidence boundaries: \ndocs/telemetry-contract.md, docs/correlation-architecture.md, docs/attack-chain-plan.md.\nValidate every alert against its source events and the run ledger as described in \ndocs/attack-detection-mapping.md or detections/README.md.",
        "type": "eql",
        "language": "eql",
        "index": [
          "apm-*-transaction*",
          "auditbeat-*",
          "endgame-*",
          "filebeat-*",
          "logs-*",
          "packetbeat-*",
          "traces-apm*",
          "winlogbeat-*",
          "-*elastic-cloud-logs-*"
        ],
        "query": "/*\r\n * Detection basis: SIGMA/SAMR PowerShell command-line flag corpus; MITRE T1059.001.\r\n * Telemetry: Sysmon EID 1, process.command_line (raw winlog.event_data.CommandLine\r\n * is NOT mapped on the lab stack and was removed - EQL verification fails on\r\n * unmapped columns). Case-insensitive comparisons.\r\n * Predicate: hidden AND (bypass|unrestricted) --OR-- encoded command. The name says\r\n * \"Encoded\": an encoded command matches without requiring hidden.\r\n * Boundary: a command-line/context signal, not proof of script contents. Parent-name\r\n * exclusions were REMOVED (a parent name does not prove provenance); expect overlap\r\n * with S3/R2 for the WMI consumer, documented as one event seen by two signals.\r\n */\r\nprocess where\r\n  winlog.event_id : \"1\"\r\n  and winlog.channel : \"Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational\"\r\n  and process.name : \"powershell.exe\"\r\n  and (\r\n    (process.command_line : (\"*-WindowStyle*Hidden*\", \"*-w*hidden*\", \"*-WindowStyle 0*\")\r\n     and process.command_line : (\"*-ExecutionPolicy*Bypass*\", \"*-ep*bypass*\", \"*-ep*unrestricted*\"))\r\n    or process.command_line : \"*-EncodedCommand*\"\r\n  )",
        "filters": [],
        "alert_suppression": {
          "group_by": [
            "host.name",
            "user.name"
          ],
          "duration": {
            "value": 60,
            "unit": "s"
          },
          "missing_fields_strategy": "suppress"
        }
      },
